# The image carries the code; the tree it is built from must not carry the
# by-products of having been tested on a Mac.
#
# __pycache__ is not cosmetic here. The compose file bind-mounts ./app read-only
# over the image's copy, so a stale .pyc from a different interpreter (a Mac's
# 3.12 against the image's 3.12 is fine; a future 3.13 is not) travels into the
# container and can shadow a module. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 in the Dockerfile
# stops the container making more of them; this stops the Mac's being shipped.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Tests, fixtures and the harness are run from the repo, never from the
# container. The container has no test runner and should not gain one: a
# container that can run tests is a container whose image has to carry them.
tests/
.venv/
venv/

# The operator's file, and the material the deploy script installs on the NAS.
# These are bind-mounted, not baked: an image that carried a private key would
# leak it into every `docker save` and every layer cache.
#
# There is no `expected/` entry any more (item 90): the drift check no longer
# carries a copy of the fleet inside the thing that grades the fleet.
.env
ssh/
data/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
